WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
A Notice to Our Customers

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
The store will be closed while 
our employees are on summer vacation.

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.430
Management

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:02.430
Huh?

00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:04.650
Did our brother and Ren go out?

00:00:04.650 --> 00:00:06.240
Yeah, to the hospital.

00:00:06.240 --> 00:00:09.570
I thought his hand had gotten a lot better.

00:00:09.910 --> 00:00:11.900
It's not that. It's his head.

00:00:11.900 --> 00:00:14.130
Oh, right. His regular checkup.

00:00:14.130 --> 00:00:15.600
Why did he suddenly decide to go?

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.230
Last time, he didn't go, even 
though he'd made an appointment.

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:23.080
He left without a fuss today. 
Ren dragged him by the hand.

00:00:23.330 --> 00:00:24.770
We're going out.

00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:27.010
Huh? What is this? A date?

00:00:27.790 --> 00:00:30.710
Yeah, I can imagine that.

00:00:30.710 --> 00:00:33.840
We were right to ask him to accompany him.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:44.100
<i>Kaidou Haru was brought in on the brink 
of death exactly seven years ago.</i>

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:46.650
<i>His face was swollen from his injuries.</i>

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:50.210
<i>It was so bad that not even 
his family recognized him.</i>

00:00:50.670 --> 00:00:54.110
<i>He finally awoke one month later.</i>

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:58.820
It sure is hot again today.

00:00:58.820 --> 00:01:01.000
Here. Take one.

00:01:03.130 --> 00:01:03.950
<i>Who is he?</i>

00:02:35.510 --> 00:02:37.240
Kaidou?

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:37.760
Yes.

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:39.430
Now I remember.

00:02:39.430 --> 00:02:43.350
You're that guy who made 
a mess of the nurse's station.

00:02:43.350 --> 00:02:46.440
You looked awful when you were brought in.

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.770
But the moment the swelling in your face went 
down, all the nurses were fighting over you.

00:02:51.080 --> 00:02:53.390
Um, I'm here for a regular checkup today.

00:02:53.390 --> 00:02:54.950
Oh, right.

00:02:55.320 --> 00:02:59.550
Though, you called it "regular," but this is 
your first one since you left the hospital.

00:02:59.550 --> 00:03:00.280
Yes.

00:03:00.550 --> 00:03:02.840
Well, there's nothing wrong with you.

00:03:02.840 --> 00:03:06.290
That's good news. Thank you very much.

00:03:06.290 --> 00:03:08.790
Not at first glance, anyway.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:09.530
Huh?

00:03:10.000 --> 00:03:14.210
People often suffer amnesia after accidents.

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:17.760
But when those lost memories return,

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.390
the victims feel like they've 
suddenly gone back in time.

00:03:23.190 --> 00:03:26.680
The accident was a shock,

00:03:27.030 --> 00:03:28.680
but it's been seven years.

00:03:28.680 --> 00:03:30.630
I can't keep letting it get me down.

00:03:30.630 --> 00:03:33.640
Yeah, and besides, that's not my job.

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.510
Huh?

00:03:34.510 --> 00:03:37.440
You have an appointment 
with Mori-sensei, right?

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.440
He'll take care of the rest.

00:03:39.660 --> 00:03:41.450
Take care of the rest?

00:03:42.230 --> 00:03:43.610
Uh...

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:47.350
If you don't take it, it's going to melt.

00:03:47.350 --> 00:03:51.340
I don't accept food from strangers. 
I don't have any reason to.

00:03:52.220 --> 00:03:56.380
Then let's say it's a treat 
from Kashiwagi-sensei.

00:03:56.380 --> 00:03:57.880
You know Mikiko?

00:03:58.250 --> 00:04:00.610
Everyone here knows her.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.630
She's our hospital's lawyer.

00:04:03.840 --> 00:04:04.900
I see.

00:04:04.900 --> 00:04:07.180
Oh, and this is who I am.

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.640
Psychotherapist

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.640
Mori Kazushi

00:04:08.010 --> 00:04:10.640
Psychosomatic Medicine

00:04:09.120 --> 00:04:10.640
A psychotherapist?

00:04:11.260 --> 00:04:13.320
Do you know what a counselor is?

00:04:13.320 --> 00:04:16.270
Oh, yeah. Is Haru your patient?

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.150
That's right.

00:04:18.150 --> 00:04:21.780
He's supposed to have a counseling 
appointment after his checkup.

00:04:21.980 --> 00:04:24.650
Well, he's one tough cookie...

00:04:24.650 --> 00:04:26.490
Ren, thanks for waiting.

00:04:26.910 --> 00:04:29.540
I paid my bill, so let's go home.

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:31.220
That was quick.

00:04:31.220 --> 00:04:34.760
Of course it was. 
There's nothing wrong with me.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:35.880
What about counseling?

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.380
They said I don't have to come anymore 
since there's nothing wrong with me.

00:04:42.420 --> 00:04:44.020
What is it? Are you hungry?

00:04:44.580 --> 00:04:46.450
You were right.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.060
See?

00:04:49.410 --> 00:04:51.640
Hey, Haru-kun. Long time, no see.

00:04:51.640 --> 00:04:53.270
Huh?! No way! Why?!

00:04:53.820 --> 00:04:58.770
Apparently you've always been 
a good liar, but he's a pro, too.

00:04:59.310 --> 00:05:03.410
It's obvious you were trying 
to skip your counseling session.

00:05:03.980 --> 00:05:06.140
I couldn't wait, so I came to see you.

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.000
Shall we go?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.870
W-Wait...

00:05:09.060 --> 00:05:11.380
Ren! Ren!

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.170
I'll wait until you're finished.

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.410
Sorry, Haru. I have work.

00:05:16.410 --> 00:05:17.880
I'll be at Mikiko's place.

00:05:17.880 --> 00:05:19.380
What?!

00:05:21.320 --> 00:05:25.340
Was that your new younger brother?

00:05:25.340 --> 00:05:29.890
Mori-sensei, I'm sure Mikiko-san
has told you all about him.

00:05:29.890 --> 00:05:32.010
What do they need 
to hear from me now?

00:05:32.460 --> 00:05:34.580
Don't be so mean.

00:05:34.580 --> 00:05:36.260
This is a counseling session.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:39.580
There's no point if we don't 
speak to each other directly.

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:41.520
I see you're as rebellious as ever.

00:05:42.190 --> 00:05:44.590
Ren-kun, was it?

00:05:44.590 --> 00:05:48.280
He's such a good boy, to accompany 
his brother to the hospital.

00:05:49.090 --> 00:05:52.030
He doesn't seem like a modern-day boy, 
but that's part of his charm.

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:56.560
Above all, I can tell he loves 
you more than anything.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:06:00.920
Ren is important to me, too. I love him.

00:06:00.920 --> 00:06:04.570
It's really cute how he's 
not like a modern-day kid.

00:06:04.570 --> 00:06:06.050
<i>Wow, he's totally in love with him.</i>

00:06:07.030 --> 00:06:10.050
By the way, I heard your 
memories have returned.

00:06:10.740 --> 00:06:13.810
And your checkup didn't find 
anything, either. That's good news.

00:06:14.140 --> 00:06:16.310
Yeah, thanks.

00:06:16.640 --> 00:06:19.340
You're taking care of your 
three school-aged brothers

00:06:19.340 --> 00:06:22.330
and handling the housework while working.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:23.820
You're a model older brother.

00:06:27.280 --> 00:06:28.810
<i>This expression...</i>

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:34.450
So why hasn't the family man and 
eldest brother of the Kaidou family

00:06:34.450 --> 00:06:39.330
gone to visit his parents' graves even once?

00:06:40.570 --> 00:06:42.840
Hello, Mikiko-san?

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:47.590
Sorry. It didn't go very well.

00:06:47.900 --> 00:06:52.070
Darn... Maybe taking Ren away 
from him was a mistake.

00:06:52.070 --> 00:06:54.850
Was he too angry to talk?

00:06:55.340 --> 00:06:58.500
He did tell me about his brothers.

00:06:59.010 --> 00:07:02.860
Could you tell him to come 
see me if he ever feels like it?

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:06.130
<i>I'd like to talk to his 
youngest brother, too.</i>

00:07:06.130 --> 00:07:08.110
What? Is there a problem?

00:07:08.110 --> 00:07:10.360
<i>I have to respect my 
patient's confidentiality.</i>

00:07:10.760 --> 00:07:11.730
Sheesh!

00:07:11.730 --> 00:07:13.870
<i>I'll call you later.</i>

00:07:14.350 --> 00:07:15.800
<i>Good grief.</i>

00:07:15.800 --> 00:07:19.250
<i>Anyway, those two seemed rather close</i>

00:07:19.250 --> 00:07:22.250
<i>for two boys who became 
brothers so recently.</i>

00:07:23.180 --> 00:07:27.470
So then Ren left without me!

00:07:27.470 --> 00:07:28.760
Don't you think that's mean?

00:07:29.270 --> 00:07:30.260
Don't you?

00:07:30.770 --> 00:07:35.240
Hey, oldest brother.
Stop complaining to the family dog.

00:07:35.870 --> 00:07:39.780
My brothers are so cold. 
Don't you think so, Tanuki?

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:43.270
Dogs don't like being smothered, Brother.

00:07:44.130 --> 00:07:47.780
By the way, what's Ren 
doing for Mikiko-san?

00:07:49.030 --> 00:07:54.280
Making copies and organizing 
documents. Sometimes he interprets.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:54.280
Hot...

00:07:54.520 --> 00:07:57.320
You got a clean bill of 
health from your checkup

00:07:57.320 --> 00:08:00.920
and took the day off 
because of your injury,

00:08:01.650 --> 00:08:04.340
but it's meaningless if Ren has work.

00:08:04.340 --> 00:08:06.450
By the way, how's your hand?

00:08:06.450 --> 00:08:10.800
Mostly healed. Your schedules for 
the week should be okay, right?

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.950
Yeah. Ren doesn't know 
where we're going, right?

00:08:13.950 --> 00:08:16.760
It's a surprise. Don't spoil it.

00:08:17.000 --> 00:08:18.140
Oh, Ren-kun.

00:08:18.140 --> 00:08:19.480
Perfect timing.

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:20.390
On your way home?

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:24.250
Hello. Do you need something?

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:26.920
Well, the café has been closed for a while.

00:08:26.920 --> 00:08:28.400
How is Haru-chan's injury?

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:32.400
Haru's probably home already. I'll go get—

00:08:32.400 --> 00:08:34.010
Oh, that's okay!

00:08:34.010 --> 00:08:35.910
We wanted to talk to you!

00:08:36.180 --> 00:08:39.270
We can't ask him this.

00:08:39.270 --> 00:08:41.890
I'm sure Haru-chan would 
find a way out of answering.

00:08:41.890 --> 00:08:44.670
He never tells us the truth.

00:08:44.990 --> 00:08:49.170
Ren-kun, are Haru-chan and 
that Kiyoka woman dating?

00:08:50.890 --> 00:08:51.670
Huh?

00:08:52.420 --> 00:08:54.170
I don't think so.

00:08:54.170 --> 00:08:57.680
What?! Then why did he 
refuse to meet my niece?

00:08:58.110 --> 00:08:58.750
Who knows?

00:08:58.750 --> 00:09:00.290
What a problem...

00:09:00.290 --> 00:09:03.680
If I tell her I don't know why, 
then she'll yell at me.

00:09:01.180 --> 00:09:09.190
Rage
Rage

00:09:01.390 --> 00:09:06.130
<i>All the female attention 
Haru receives is nothing new,</i>

00:09:06.130 --> 00:09:08.420
<i>but why do they have to keep coming?</i>

00:09:08.420 --> 00:09:09.190
Ren?

00:09:10.300 --> 00:09:11.180
Welcome home.

00:09:11.180 --> 00:09:12.710
What are you all doing here?

00:09:12.710 --> 00:09:13.710
Oh, um...

00:09:13.710 --> 00:09:14.950
Oh! We came to check up on you!

00:09:14.950 --> 00:09:17.770
Haru-chan, that's from all of us!

00:09:17.770 --> 00:09:20.560
We'll be back once you 
reopen the café, okay?

00:09:20.560 --> 00:09:21.300
What was that?

00:09:21.300 --> 00:09:22.200
Who knows?

00:09:23.250 --> 00:09:26.380
Ren, are you working 
every day this week?

00:09:26.380 --> 00:09:28.710
No, not this week.

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:29.830
Really?

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.210
What?

00:09:31.590 --> 00:09:34.380
I'm taking the entire week 
off work for summer break.

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.220
Don't you want to go somewhere, too?

00:09:36.440 --> 00:09:37.840
Not really.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.940
Yeah, no, it's fine.

00:09:40.940 --> 00:09:43.320
I expected you to say that.

00:09:46.370 --> 00:09:47.100
Huh?

00:09:47.480 --> 00:09:50.360
Squeeze.

00:09:48.900 --> 00:09:50.360
Uh... Ren?

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.410
I like what's going on,

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:55.490
but why are you hugging me with 
such a scary look on your face?

00:09:55.490 --> 00:09:57.360
My face always looks like this.

00:09:57.720 --> 00:10:01.620
Oh, did Ohtomo-san and her 
friends say something to you?

00:10:01.620 --> 00:10:02.370
Not really.

00:10:03.090 --> 00:10:05.690
They mostly talked about you.

00:10:05.690 --> 00:10:06.370
Huh?

00:10:06.860 --> 00:10:10.380
Sorry I couldn't stay with you at the 
hospital until you were finished.

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:17.130
It's fine. I can never say 
no to Mikiko-san, either.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:23.790
<i>No one's better at buttering 
me up than this kid.</i>

00:10:28.330 --> 00:10:28.890
Huh?

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:32.550
What? You finally feel like 
sleeping in here again?

00:10:32.550 --> 00:10:37.860
Your hand has mostly healed, 
and your checkup didn't find anything.

00:10:38.140 --> 00:10:41.490
So there's no reason for me 
to sleep alone anymore.

00:10:41.490 --> 00:10:42.420
Yeah.

00:10:42.420 --> 00:10:45.620
Sleeping alone was getting so lonely.

00:10:45.990 --> 00:10:48.340
I thought about going to 
your room so many times.

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:52.530
Haru, when can I have sex with you?

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:54.590
Wh-What?!

00:10:54.590 --> 00:10:56.840
Creep Creep

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:56.840
I've heard men can have sex with—

00:10:56.840 --> 00:10:58.590
Whoa, just shut up!

00:10:58.590 --> 00:11:00.510
Go to sleep, you filthy little kid!

00:11:01.140 --> 00:11:01.890
What about sex?

00:11:01.890 --> 00:11:03.100
No!

00:11:03.900 --> 00:11:06.600
Why? Because I'm a guy?

00:11:06.870 --> 00:11:08.230
No.

00:11:08.560 --> 00:11:09.680
Then wh—

00:11:10.110 --> 00:11:12.090
Because you're still a kid,

00:11:12.090 --> 00:11:15.730
and you're so stupid and naïve, 
it makes my head hurt.

00:11:18.240 --> 00:11:19.360
You...

00:11:24.930 --> 00:11:28.120
Where did you learn that trick?

00:11:28.570 --> 00:11:32.200
I might ground you, 
depending on your answer.

00:11:32.200 --> 00:11:33.000
What?

00:11:33.800 --> 00:11:35.500
Are you stupid?

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:38.250
They're all things you've done to me.

00:11:40.960 --> 00:11:42.580
What's wrong with me?

00:11:42.580 --> 00:11:43.610
I'm so embarrassed!

00:11:43.610 --> 00:11:45.050
Why are you getting embarrassed now?

00:11:47.810 --> 00:11:50.610
Haru, where are we?

00:11:48.600 --> 00:11:54.560
It's hot

00:11:49.020 --> 00:11:54.560
It smells like seawater

00:11:49.480 --> 00:11:54.560
It's sticky

00:11:51.140 --> 00:11:54.560
Sorry... I brought you 
to the beach as a surprise.

00:11:54.890 --> 00:11:56.320
I'm sorry.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:01.320
What? Ren still won't come out of that tent?

00:12:01.320 --> 00:12:03.770
Isn't it your first time at the beach?

00:12:03.770 --> 00:12:06.830
It's bigger than a lake. 
You'll have fun swimming in it.

00:12:07.490 --> 00:12:10.830
Lake Louise is a hundred times 
prettier than this place.

00:12:11.420 --> 00:12:14.830
Who swims next to a glacier? That'd kill you!

00:12:15.350 --> 00:12:18.800
How long are you guys 
going to keep that up?

00:12:18.800 --> 00:12:20.050
Natsuo?

00:12:20.050 --> 00:12:23.080
Japan's food stands have evolved lately.

00:12:23.630 --> 00:12:25.240
Here, Ren. You want some?

00:12:26.640 --> 00:12:28.040
See? He came out.

00:12:28.040 --> 00:12:30.890
Come to think of it, 
he hadn't had breakfast yet.

00:12:31.120 --> 00:12:35.220
Huh? Bro, I thought you said Ikuyoshi 
and Kiyoka were coming, too.

00:12:35.220 --> 00:12:39.400
Yeah, Kiyo said she'd come 
as part of a company trip.

00:12:39.660 --> 00:12:40.940
I'll try calling her.

00:12:40.940 --> 00:12:43.540
No, wait. That's probably them.

00:12:43.540 --> 00:12:44.150
Huh?

00:12:53.370 --> 00:12:54.670
Maybe I won't call.

00:12:55.450 --> 00:12:57.230
I found Haru-san!

00:12:57.230 --> 00:12:59.670
Seems like it's too late, though.

00:12:59.670 --> 00:13:01.010
I glad I found you!

00:13:01.010 --> 00:13:04.140
I was just thinking there's a group 
of hot guys on the beach,

00:13:04.140 --> 00:13:05.680
and it turned out to be you guys!

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:09.400
I'm glad you guys were so easy to find.

00:13:09.400 --> 00:13:10.180
You, too.

00:13:10.420 --> 00:13:12.740
Haru, you're late.

00:13:12.740 --> 00:13:15.640
Is this a company trip for 
your shop on Second Street?

00:13:15.640 --> 00:13:17.370
That's right.

00:13:17.370 --> 00:13:20.910
Oh, my, he's handsome!
Kiyoka, introduce us!

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:22.870
I'm Tamaki.

00:13:22.870 --> 00:13:23.870
Hello.

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:28.250
Why are you so unhappy?

00:13:28.630 --> 00:13:33.070
I'm not. I'm just tired because 
I was woken up early this morning

00:13:33.070 --> 00:13:35.960
and brought here without 
being told where we were going.

00:13:36.270 --> 00:13:38.090
You're one to talk.

00:13:38.090 --> 00:13:40.690
You slept soundly in the car.

00:13:40.690 --> 00:13:43.460
You didn't even notice 
when I joined you guys.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:46.500
Haru, where are your sunglasses?

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.220
I forgot them in the car.

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:53.230
You idiot. The sun will damage your eyes.

00:13:53.230 --> 00:13:54.730
Here, you can borrow mine.

00:13:54.730 --> 00:13:55.980
Thanks.

00:13:55.980 --> 00:13:57.970
Apparently they were friends in high school.

00:13:57.970 --> 00:13:58.810
Are you jealous?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:14:03.480
Not really. Kiyoka's just a friend to him.

00:14:03.770 --> 00:14:07.490
I guess. She's beautiful, but it's different.

00:14:08.550 --> 00:14:12.600
Kiyoka said Haru is a ladies' 
man through and through.

00:14:12.600 --> 00:14:14.020
I agree.

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.500
But you're special?

00:14:18.200 --> 00:14:20.000
Watch out for Haru.

00:14:20.450 --> 00:14:24.280
His family's more important 
to him than his lovers.

00:14:25.670 --> 00:14:26.500
Well—

00:14:26.500 --> 00:14:27.260
Ren?

00:14:28.000 --> 00:14:31.760
What, are you hungry? I made rice balls.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:34.570
I'll put sunscreen on you while you eat.

00:14:34.870 --> 00:14:38.770
Well, as long as you're his brother, 
you'll be his number one.

00:14:38.970 --> 00:14:39.970
Good luck.

00:14:40.740 --> 00:14:41.770
What?

00:14:44.920 --> 00:14:48.730
Uh-oh. Active hosts sure do work fast.

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:51.180
Were you like that, too?

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:51.780
Huh?!

00:14:51.780 --> 00:14:53.690
Ren, that was someone else!

00:14:53.690 --> 00:14:56.500
I'm not the same person now!

00:14:57.210 --> 00:14:58.250
So I'm right.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:01.980
Anyway, where did Aki and Shima go?

00:15:01.980 --> 00:15:06.670
They went to buy snacks with Iku.

00:15:06.670 --> 00:15:09.260
Let's go swimming when they get back.

00:15:12.400 --> 00:15:13.700
Ren, what's wrong?

00:15:14.010 --> 00:15:17.140
This feels gross under my feet.

00:15:17.380 --> 00:15:19.820
Oh, yeah. You'll get used to it.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.920
Want to go out to sea?

00:15:22.920 --> 00:15:26.030
It's crowded and hard 
to swim in the shallows.

00:15:27.100 --> 00:15:29.210
Did he say it was his 
first time at the beach?

00:15:29.750 --> 00:15:32.030
Oh, Ren's? That's what he said, right?

00:15:32.030 --> 00:15:37.490
2.0 Visual Acuity

00:15:32.570 --> 00:15:36.430
I thought I saw him being led out to sea.

00:15:37.090 --> 00:15:40.790
I forgot to ask, but can Ren swim?

00:15:41.800 --> 00:15:42.790
Dunno.

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:47.780
Welcome back.

00:15:47.780 --> 00:15:51.760
Ren, you should've 
told me you can't swim!

00:15:51.760 --> 00:15:54.140
The result.

00:15:52.190 --> 00:15:53.140
The result...

00:15:55.030 --> 00:15:55.760
There.

00:15:56.810 --> 00:15:59.080
Shima, you're not going to swim?

00:15:59.080 --> 00:16:00.700
I'm watching our stuff.

00:16:00.700 --> 00:16:02.460
Why don't you go swim, then?

00:16:02.460 --> 00:16:03.790
I'll switch with you.

00:16:04.640 --> 00:16:06.770
Are you sure you don't 
need to stay with them?

00:16:06.770 --> 00:16:09.680
It's fine. I gave them my club's card.

00:16:11.330 --> 00:16:15.280
By the way, do you know a lady 
lawyer named Kashiwagi something?

00:16:16.020 --> 00:16:17.850
Mikiko-san? Of course I know her.

00:16:17.850 --> 00:16:21.580
Not only is she our landlady, but she's 
been looking after us for a long time.

00:16:21.580 --> 00:16:23.790
She suddenly called me the other day.

00:16:24.630 --> 00:16:26.800
She'd looked up my workplace, 
my current address,

00:16:26.800 --> 00:16:30.500
and even my phone number. It was scary.

00:16:30.500 --> 00:16:33.300
I thought she was trying 
to collect on my dad's debt.

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:36.270
It wouldn't surprise me if she was.

00:16:37.720 --> 00:16:42.110
That wasn't it, though. 
We talked about your brother.

00:16:44.230 --> 00:16:49.320
Apparently, Haru hasn't visited his 
parents' graves once in seven years.

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.540
Not that I can criticize anyone.

00:16:52.540 --> 00:16:54.920
His not going isn't a problem.

00:16:54.920 --> 00:16:57.170
Aki and I can go.

00:16:58.270 --> 00:17:00.320
Why don't you take him with you once?

00:17:00.320 --> 00:17:01.990
Isn't Ren worried about it, too?

00:17:03.240 --> 00:17:05.330
We don't talk about that.

00:17:06.360 --> 00:17:08.770
It'd be a different story if Ren 
said he wanted to go, though.

00:17:08.770 --> 00:17:10.460
Don't you think it's strange?

00:17:10.460 --> 00:17:11.840
There's nothing strange about it.

00:17:12.450 --> 00:17:16.340
He thinks it's his fault our parents died.

00:17:16.990 --> 00:17:19.720
Our grandparents said the same thing.

00:17:19.720 --> 00:17:20.640
Yikes.

00:17:21.740 --> 00:17:24.100
Ren feels responsible, too.

00:17:24.840 --> 00:17:28.990
Our brother wouldn't have gone 
to Canada if not for him,

00:17:28.990 --> 00:17:32.020
so the accident wouldn't have happened.

00:17:32.020 --> 00:17:33.970
What a pain in the ass.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:35.610
It's not like it's their fault.

00:17:36.230 --> 00:17:38.010
You should tell them that.

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:43.170
I can't. When he woke up 
after a month, Aki blamed him.

00:17:43.170 --> 00:17:44.870
And I didn't stop him.

00:17:45.770 --> 00:17:50.380
He disappeared for a while after that.

00:17:51.450 --> 00:17:55.380
Neither Aki nor I want 
to go through that again.

00:17:58.180 --> 00:17:59.390
Aki, what are you doing?

00:17:59.390 --> 00:18:01.390
I'm getting you used to the water.

00:18:01.740 --> 00:18:02.740
Stop that!

00:18:02.740 --> 00:18:06.390
You don't want to put your face in 
the water? What are you, a dog?

00:18:06.740 --> 00:18:10.850
There's no telling who's been in there! 
I don't want to put my face in it!

00:18:10.850 --> 00:18:13.090
What do you think the ocean is?!

00:18:13.660 --> 00:18:15.400
Okay, okay. That's enough.

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.190
Ren, you must be tired. Let's take a break.

00:18:18.190 --> 00:18:19.910
There, there.

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:23.290
Shima's probably tired of waiting for...

00:18:29.800 --> 00:18:30.550
Haru?

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:32.850
Haru? Haru!

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:42.050
Bro?

00:18:42.050 --> 00:18:44.020
Ren Ren, are you okay?

00:18:44.310 --> 00:18:47.430
You idiot, Aki! Did you see that?

00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:51.150
Ren can do anything if he tries!

00:18:51.150 --> 00:18:52.150
Right, Ren?

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:55.150
Ren, what's wrong?

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:57.460
Did you swallow sea water?

00:18:57.460 --> 00:18:58.900
You're unbelievable.

00:18:59.150 --> 00:19:00.910
Headbutt.

00:19:01.210 --> 00:19:02.760
And stay down there!

00:19:02.760 --> 00:19:04.570
What an idiot.

00:19:06.660 --> 00:19:07.250
What?

00:19:07.590 --> 00:19:12.000
Are you stupid? There are some 
jokes you should never make.

00:19:12.340 --> 00:19:14.650
I can't believe you can't tell 
which is which at your age.

00:19:14.650 --> 00:19:18.900
I said I was sorry!

00:19:18.900 --> 00:19:20.010
Where did he go?

00:19:20.010 --> 00:19:24.510
I don't know. Ren's not a little kid.

00:19:24.510 --> 00:19:26.520
Aw, jeez!

00:19:27.830 --> 00:19:31.020
Aren't there any better guys around?

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:34.660
What's wrong with all of them? 
They're so frail.

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:39.030
Katrina

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:39.030
Koko

00:19:31.020 --> 00:19:39.030
Tamaki

00:19:34.660 --> 00:19:36.140
Oh, stop.

00:19:36.140 --> 00:19:39.030
I don't like musclebound idiots like you.

00:19:39.030 --> 00:19:42.430
I don't want someone who 
looks just like me, either!

00:19:42.430 --> 00:19:47.790
I want a slightly wizened man 
who doesn't fit in with society.

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.210
Ren-kun, how's this? Is it good?

00:19:47.210 --> 00:19:47.790
Yeah.

00:19:48.280 --> 00:19:50.630
But young boys are nice once in a while.

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:52.190
He's so cute!

00:19:52.190 --> 00:19:54.590
All your brothers are so handsome, too.

00:19:54.590 --> 00:19:58.050
You get to look at those faces 
all the time. I'm so jealous.

00:19:58.490 --> 00:20:00.790
Haru spends most of his time in the café.

00:20:00.790 --> 00:20:02.550
You can come anytime.

00:20:02.800 --> 00:20:05.300
Oh, my! You mean we can go?!

00:20:06.310 --> 00:20:08.560
Ren-kun, you're such a good boy!

00:20:09.330 --> 00:20:11.280
Ren, what are you doing?

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:13.560
What is this?

00:20:09.680 --> 00:20:13.560
A brothel?!

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:16.570
Um...

00:20:16.930 --> 00:20:20.080
I'm sorry, okay? 
Will you come back with me?

00:20:20.080 --> 00:20:22.300
Everyone else is worried, too.

00:20:22.300 --> 00:20:24.570
I'm really sorry!

00:20:24.850 --> 00:20:29.180
Men only apologize like that 
when they're desperate.

00:20:29.180 --> 00:20:32.030
They only do it because 
they have no pride.

00:20:32.030 --> 00:20:33.790
You should punish him.

00:20:33.790 --> 00:20:35.830
Shut up, all of you!

00:20:35.880 --> 00:20:37.340
Clench.

00:20:36.540 --> 00:20:37.340
That's right...

00:20:37.940 --> 00:20:40.020
I guess I could punish him.

00:20:40.020 --> 00:20:42.410
At this rate, you'll never 
be more than a mongrel.

00:20:42.410 --> 00:20:45.840
Ren? Why are you raising your fist?

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:47.540
Close your eyes.

00:20:45.840 --> 00:20:51.350
Rumble

00:20:47.540 --> 00:20:51.350
Okay, fine! But make it just one, okay?

00:21:00.700 --> 00:21:02.990
<i>Uh... What?</i>

00:21:02.990 --> 00:21:07.130
<i>This is a rather delightful punishment...</i>

00:21:08.260 --> 00:21:08.870
Re—

00:21:08.870 --> 00:21:10.120
Chomp

00:21:10.320 --> 00:21:11.370
"Chomp"?

00:21:12.370 --> 00:21:15.870
Blood.

00:21:13.460 --> 00:21:15.100
You bit my tongue!

00:21:15.870 --> 00:21:17.750
Why did he kiss him?!

00:21:16.110 --> 00:21:17.750
What a terrifying child!

00:21:19.560 --> 00:21:23.220
Shima, Ren, we're going home.

00:21:24.960 --> 00:21:27.460
Did something happen to his tongue?

00:21:27.460 --> 00:21:29.110
It's no big deal.

00:21:29.110 --> 00:21:34.270
Haruko told me before to use the 
carrot-and-stick method with Haru.

00:21:34.530 --> 00:21:37.910
Oh, right. I think I know what you did.

00:21:38.320 --> 00:21:39.770
Ren-kun!

00:21:40.200 --> 00:21:42.780
Ren-kun, see you next time!

00:21:43.110 --> 00:21:44.740
Bye!

00:21:45.260 --> 00:21:49.530
So, how was your first time at the beach?

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:56.260
Next year, I'll learn to swim 
so I can beat Haru.

00:21:56.260 --> 00:21:58.930
Don't you think you're 
setting the bar too low?

00:23:30.090 --> 00:23:40.340
Next Time
